        ],
        "value": "As a review article, the approach involves a structured synthesis of literature rather than new empirical experimentation. The authors systematically: 1) Summarize clinical trial data associating specific gut microbiota profiles with ICI response in solid tumors; 2) Compare the advantages and limitations of traditional 2D cell lines, animal xenografts, and emerging 3D organoid models; 3) Detail the methodologies for generating immune-reactive organoids (endogenous retention vs. autologous co-culture); 4) Review selected studies demonstrating the application of these organoids in testing microbial metabolites and immunotherapies; 5) Discuss future perspectives and challenges in integrating microbiome components into organoid cultures.",
        "role": "evidence",
