      {
        "atom_id": "atom::57eb466c11cee4074bef8508",
        "source_handle": "P0172",
        "field_path": [
          "study_summary_A",
          "research_scope"
        ],
        "value": "The review focuses on the application of intestinal organoids (including patient-derived, stem cell-derived, and cancer cell line-derived models) as in vitro tools to study the interactions between the gut microbiota and the Tumor Microenvironment (TME), particularly in colorectal cancer. It covers mechanistic insights into microbial dysbiosis, metabolite regulation, immune modulation, and clinical translation scenarios such as drug screening and biomarker discovery.",
